  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "`src/sites.rs#fn[validate_review]` takes `errors: &mut Vec<String>`, so it is a site of `requirements.ci.errors`. It meets the obligations.\n\nEarly-exit matches:\n- **Read failure, JSON parse failure, non-object value.** These three `return`s each report one error and stop. Every later check reads the file content, the parsed value or its object fields. These are parse failures of a single evidence file, which the requirement treats as one failed check. No independent check is skipped.\n- **`crate::evidence_format::view` failure.** The function returns after reporting the decoding error. The only check that could still run is `crate::evidence_format::check_native`, which does not use the view's result. However, `check_native` calls `versioned_fields` on the same value that made `view` fail, and it would report that failure again as \"cannot check SDK evidence\". Returning avoids reporting one failure twice. The requirement also allows an error to report only the first decoding problem in a file.\n- **`return` in `let Some(inputs) = array_field(...) else { return; }`.** A missing or invalid `inputs` field has already been reported by `array_field`. The remaining checks are the per-input validation, \"inputs must select the site\" and \"inputs must include the declaration\". All of them depend on the contents of `inputs`. Every independent check has already run before this point. These are the `requirement`/`file`/`item` fields, queries, fixmes, applies, determination, rationale and the `applies`/`determination` consistency check.\n- **`?` operators on `fixme.get(\"item\")?`, `.as_str()?` and `fixme.get(\"commentary\")?`.** These sit inside a closure that returns `Option<SiteFixme>`. They do not leave the function. A malformed entry makes `parsed` `None`, which yields exactly one \"fixmes must be an array of objects…\" error. The other checks still run.\n\nBeyond the matches, each field check, the queries and fixmes comparisons, the `applies` and determination checks and the rationale check push their own error and continue. The `determination` false, `applies` false and `Fixme` validation errors describe different conditions, so no failure is reported twice.\n\nI found no gap.",
  "inputs": [
    {
      "file": "src/sites.rs",
      "item": "fn[validate_review]",
      "hash": "33c526658278483a59a7e6ca8fa33bacae1c40ab5f84cbc313284d04f1c7328f"
    },
    {
      "requirements": "requirements.ci.errors",
      "matches": [
        "requirements.ci.errors"
      ],
      "text": [
        ":::::{req} errors",
        "Repository validation MUST continue after a failed check and report every failed",
        "check it finds in one run, each as a {term}`requirements.ci.validation_error`.",
        "This is a convention for every validation error; the requirement for each check",
        "states which conditions that check reports. A file that cannot be parsed, such as",
        "a malformed `habeas.toml`, `book.toml`, or evidence file, is one failed check:",
        "its error MAY report only the first parse or decoding problem in that file, and",
        "checks that do not depend on its contents MUST still run.",
        "",
        "The code that sequences the repository's checks carries out the first paragraph.",
        "A repository-validation function that collects validation errors MUST hold them",
        "in a parameter or local variable named `errors`, and a function with such a",
        "variable is a site below; authoring code that collects errors only to abort is",
        "not one. After one of its checks fails, a site MUST still run every later check",
        "that does not depend on the failed check's result, including later checks in the",
        "same loop iteration, and MUST NOT report one failure twice.",
        "",
        "::::{sites} error_accumulators",
        "```yaml",
        "language: rust",
        "paths: [src, crates/trust-but-verify/src]",
        "exclude: [src/authoring/inputs.rs, src/authoring/tools.rs]",
        "rule:",
        "  kind: function_item",
        "  has:",
        "    stopBy: { kind: function_item }",
        "    any:",
        "      - kind: parameter",
        "        has: { field: pattern, regex: \"^errors$\" }",
        "      - kind: let_declaration",
        "        has: { field: pattern, regex: \"^errors$\" }",
        "  not:",
        "    inside:",
        "      stopBy: end",
        "      kind: mod_item",
        "      has: { field: name, regex: \"^tests$\" }",
        "match:",
        "  - \"fn check(value: &str, errors: &mut Vec<String>) {}\"",
        "  - |",
        "    fn run() {",
        "        let mut errors: BTreeSet<String> = BTreeSet::new();",
        "        check(\"\", &mut errors);",
        "    }",
        "no_match:",
        "  - \"fn check(value: &str, discovery_errors: &mut Vec<String>) {}\"",
        "  - |",
        "    fn run() {",
        "        let mut problems = Vec::new();",
        "        check(\"\", &mut problems);",
        "    }",
        "  - |",
        "    mod tests {",
        "        fn check(errors: &mut Vec<String>) {}",
        "    }",
        "```",
        "::::",
        "",
        "::::{violations} early_exits",
        "```yaml",
        "language: rust",
        "paths: [src, crates/trust-but-verify/src]",
        "within: error_accumulators",
        "rule:",
        "  any:",
        "    - kind: try_expression",
        "    - kind: return_expression",
        "    - kind: continue_expression",
        "    - kind: break_expression",
        "match:",
        "  - |",
        "    fn check(v: &Value, errors: &mut Vec<String>) -> Option<u8> {",
        "        let n = v.as_u64()?;",
        "        if v.is_null() { errors.push(\"null\".into()); }",
        "        Some(n as u8)",
        "    }",
        "  - |",
        "    fn check(items: &[Value], errors: &mut Vec<String>) {",
        "        for item in items {",
        "            if !item.is_object() { errors.push(\"object\".into()); continue; }",
        "            if item.is_null() { errors.push(\"null\".into()); }",
        "        }",
        "    }",
        "  - |",
        "    fn check(v: &Value, errors: &mut Vec<String>) {",
        "        if !v.is_object() { errors.push(\"object\".into()); return; }",
        "        if v.is_null() { errors.push(\"null\".into()); }",
        "    }",
        "  - |",
        "    fn check(items: &[Value], errors: &mut Vec<String>) {",
        "        for item in items {",
        "            if !item.is_object() { errors.push(\"object\".into()); break; }",
        "        }",
        "        if items.is_empty() { errors.push(\"empty\".into()); }",
        "    }",
        "no_match:",
        "  - |",
        "    fn parse(v: &Value) -> Option<u8> {",
        "        let n = v.as_u64()?;",
        "        Some(n as u8)",
        "    }",
        "```",
        "::::",
        ":::::"
      ]
    },
